shunt (2.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Writing DNS settings no longer deletes the DHCP server. apply_topology.py
    and build_dnsmasq_conf write the same file, and the second emitted only the
    DNS half -- so changing a resolver in the interface removed the DHCP the
    downstream router leases its WAN address from, and the router went dark at
    its next renewal with nothing connecting the two events. Whichever writer
    runs last now produces a complete file, and it binds dynamically for the
